'''''Ornithopus pinnatus''''', the  '''orange birdsfoot''',<ref name=gbif/> is a plant in the [[Fabaceae]] family.<ref name=apni>{{APNI2|id=56556|name=''Ornithopus pinnatus''}}</ref> It was first described as ''Scorpiurus pinnata'' in 1768 by [[Philip Miller]] in ''The Gardeners Dictionary''.<ref name=apni/><ref name=mill>{{cite Q|Q7735861|edition=8|url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/395529}}</ref> In 1907, [[George Claridge Druce]] assigned it to the genus ''[[Ornithopus]]''.<ref name=apni/><ref name=druce/> 

It is native to Western Europe, the [[Mediterranean Region]] and [[Macaronesia]] but is found elsewhere as an introduced species.<ref>{{cite web |title=Ornithopus pinnatus |url=http://www.floraiberica.es/floraiberica/texto/pdfs/07_49%20Ornithopus.pdf |publisher=[[Flora Iberica]] |access-date=26 June 2022}}</ref><ref name=powo/><ref name="gbif">{{Cite web|title=''Ornithopus pinnatus'' (Mill.) Druce|url=https://www.gbif.org/species/5358260|access-date=2021-11-12|website=www.gbif.org|language=en}}</ref>
